Package: r-cornball-rctl
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, r-base-core (>= 4.6.0), r-api-4.0, r-cornball-janssonr, r-cornball-runix
Recommends: r-cornball-pkgstate, r-cornball-rsystemd
Description: Runix command-line interface
 A machine-drivable CLI over the Runix subsystem packages, covering read-only
 introspection and managed service mutations. In machine mode (--json) it emits
 exactly one versioned JSON envelope per invocation. Subsystem packages are
 detected at runtime, so capability introspection succeeds even where the
 pkgstate and rsystemd subsystems (Recommends) are absent.
 .
 The /usr/bin/rctl launcher uses Rscript, so the package needs no littler: it
 matches rctl's DESCRIPTION (littler is a Suggests, not an Import) and stays
 installable on the CRAN R the stack requires, where the distribution's
 R-4.3-pinned littler cannot co-install. A CRAN-R-compatible littler becomes an
 optional Recommends once one is packaged.
 .
 Experimental. Part of Runix (https://github.com/cornball-ai/runix).
